FINDINGS:
1. [BLOCKER] tests/differential_test.rs:209 — `let fresh = corpus::corpus().len()` compared against `checked_in.len()` from the same `corpus()` call, so the assertion is tautological — a vacuous gate that cannot fail — compare `sources.len()` against the on-disk count instead
2. [BLOCKER] src/bytecode/vm.rs:1026 — `.expect("an object declaration being assembled")` panics when `pending_object` is `None`, reachable from Redblue source because `def_object` keeps a single slot (src/bytecode/vm.rs:1893 overwrites it) and a `has default <expr>` compiles any expression (src/bytecode/codegen.rs:353), so a default that calls a function declaring an object clobbers the outer pending and the outer unwind panics — keep a stack of pendings and return a clean error on underflow
3. [MAJOR] tests/common/vm.rs:328 — `same_place` ignores columns for every `RuntimeError`, so the differential gate is widened to line-only for 43 corpus failures — a column regression on either VM is invisible — compare full positions or record the format limit per-failure instead of blanket-ignoring
4. [MAJOR] tests/differential_test.rs:317 — `edge_a_generated_program_only_faults_on_a_fault_that_was_injected` runs only `vm::tree_walk`, never `vm::bytecode`, so the typed-grammar invariant is unproven on the second engine — run and assert both engines per seed
5. [MAJOR] tests/common/vm.rs:546 — `edge_a_vm_built_as_a_library_does_not_print_what_the_program_said` builds `loud` with default echo-on and only asserts `take_output`, never capturing stdout, so a broken `set_echo(false)` still passes — assert silence via output capture on the echo-off path
6. [MAJOR] corpus/control-flow-0003.rb:3 — all three `else if` programs record `#label ParserError` (corpus/control-flow-0003.expected:1), and the generator only draws bare `if` (tests/common/generator.rs:440), so zero successful `else if` programs exist despite the claimed `if/else if/else` coverage — add a working `else if` success case or correct the coverage claim
7. [MINOR] tests/differential_test.rs:202 — `RB_WRITE_CORPUS=1` rewrites the checked-in `corpus/` dir inside the test while other tests read it, so a regression is laundered into goldens and parallel runs race — write only to scratch and fail on diff, never mutate `corpus_dir()` in-test
8. [MINOR] src/bytecode/vm.rs:1602 — `break_loop`/`skip_loop` only advance, and corpus/loop-forms-0012.expected:4 enshrines the no-op as success, baking the bug into goldens so a real fix breaks the corpus — mark these as known-failure expectations, not completions
REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 8
